WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.760
A converted church.

2
00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.000
A warehouse.

3
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.290
A house.

4
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.850
Sikhs have turned all three
into places of worship.

5
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.170
Each one is now a gurdwara.

6
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.690
The word means door of the Guru.

7
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.190
And every gurdwara has a kitchen.

8
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.520
Anyone who walks in, Sikh or
not, is offered a free meal.

9
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.740
So what turns an ordinary
building into a gurdwara?

10
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.020
And why does everyone eat there?

11
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.470
In this mission, you'll step inside the
prayer hall and follow a typical service,

12
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.240
from hymns to a shared sweet offering.

13
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:35.200
Then you'll trace the free
kitchen, called langar,

14
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.660
back to the early Gurus, and find
out why its food is vegetarian.

15
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:43.130
Your mission: find out what
makes a building a gurdwara,

16
00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.090
and why everyone eats there.
